  "decision": "PASS_SOURCE_GRAPH",
  "evidence_kind": "static source inspection; not runtime behavior",
  "integration_judgment": {
    "boundary": "A supervisor-service death still needs an external restart/display-reset policy; A04 proves only Executor-child death while the owner supervisor remains alive.",
    "current_failure_domain": "The MAP01 session subprocess creates the Executor and owner-thread InputOwner. A hard death of that subprocess removes both; the outer controller only knows the child process and has no display-bound release client.",
    "recovery_direction": "Move input ownership into a longer-lived supervisor/service outside the session/Executor child failure domain. Add a strict local RPC adapter in the session backend, publish the display/auth context before input authority, and on child EOF close the owner and persist verified release evidence before any new admission."
  },
